{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125827-what-s-the-point-of-being-bad","id":1125827,"title":"What's the point of being Bad?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-07T01:57:44-07:00","id":1125827,"title":"What's the point of being Bad?","content":"Not talking about Nephandi-level bad or Infernally bad; these are complex questions.<br /> <br /> I'm talking about your average Mage. Ordinary Avatar. Doesn't want to destroy the world. Largely sane. Why would they want to sacrifice humans for their magic?<br /> <br /> Yes, humans are a source of Quintessence. So are Horses. Yes, humans can be used as a focus for Maleficia, Blood and Sacrifices etc. There are many alternatives to *actual human sacrifice*. Basically I have to wonder what the incentive is to be cruel or evil. Is there any mechanical advantage? Or is it hand-waved as &quot;some people are evil and they don't need a mechanical advantage&quot;? Because evil people IRL tend to get something from it, even in a very short-sighted and idiotic way.<br /> <br /> I've yet to find any real advantage to sacrificing someone, beyond the possibility that this may count as pulling on a Mythic Thread or using a Unique Instrument if the person is suitable; easily replicated. What if human sacrifice absorbed a bit of Paradox? The idea would be that their departing Quintessence would be partly consumed by the Paradox generated, possibly obliterating their soul altogether. So if the spell is Vulgar and Successful then it absorbs the one point of Paradox. If the spell is Vulgar and Botches then it absorbs Paradox so that the backlash is 3x Highest Level Sphere, which could be a significant reduction.<br /> <br /> Or you could significantly reduce how much Quintessence you can get from animals, using a Vampire-type justification; yes an Elephant might be HUGE and it might seem logical that they'd contain a lot of Blood/Quintessence, but they are less energy-rich than a human; their soul is on a similar level to that of a dog or monkey, they just have a much much larger body to go with it. Simple, unintelligent animals would have a Quintessence of 1, smart animals (octopi, dogs, monkeys, elephants, dolphins) would have a Quintessence of 3 due to a slightly greater state of self-awareness. Now one human sacrifice is three times as potent as a dog sacrifice, which is a big enough gap that a sociopath might prefer a human...<br /> <br /> Have I missed some advantage to virgin sacrifice? Does it need a mechanical incentive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-07-2017, 05:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T02:48:43-07:00","id":1125832,"title":"","content":"&quot;Being&quot; evil is something that in my opinion happens in bad character writing, or wanting to be edgy. I prefer to see it as unempathetic towards another inidividuals, having a might is right mindset etc. and with the mindset comes the advantages. <br /> <br /> Amorality doesn't begin with human sacrifice, which is more at the &quot;depraved&quot; &quot;apathetic&quot; end of the spectrum. A moral character for example would prefer to defeat their enemies without defeat, fight them honorably etc. An amoral character could use poison gas, explosives, traps or leave mutilated corpses (or corpses in a generally bad shape, being cutin two for example) behind to disturb their enemies and weaken their morale.<br /> <br /> It only makes sense to act evil when you gain efficiency, or a psychologycal bonus from it.<br /> <br /> Even though I find the notion of sacrificing souls interisting, you have to think about what big of a crime this is. Normally, if you would sacrifice a human, you would burn up his bodily pattern and absorb his quintessence. If you would like to also render their soul, you would need in my guess at least Prime 4 and either spirit 3 or 4, depending on ST choice. <br /> <br /> Large Animals are used in sacrifices for thousands of years and an animal with somewhat the body mass of a human should give the same amount of quintessence as you are absorbing the live pattern. The benefit in human sacrifice could very well be in mythic threads, which is not to be underestimated as every difficulty reduction in an arete throw can be a significant boon. Also there is the notion that different kind of quintessence has different resonance. The essence gained from sacrificing humans would have entropic resonances, making them very usefull in destructive rituals, but less so in constructive ones.<br /> <br /> At last, I don't see any reason to lesser you paradox for human sacrifice as reality doesn't really care about what you do. If you burn the body and harness the essence with Prime 4, you can do it coincidentally, if you botch, you don't harness energy and the paradox is yours. If you would use Prime 5 to just &quot;rip away their life force&quot;, no chance of this being not vulgar, unless you are in a special reality zone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13530-queen-nihil","name":"Queen Nihil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13530_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T04:30:52-07:00","id":1125841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queen Nihil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125827-what-s-the-point-of-being-bad?p=1125832#post1125832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Being&quot; evil is something that in my opinion happens in bad character writing, or wanting to be edgy. I prefer to see it as unempathetic towards another inidividuals, having a might is right mindset etc. and with the mindset comes the advantages.<br /> <br /> Large Animals are used in sacrifices for thousands of years and an animal with somewhat the body mass of a human should give the same amount of quintessence as you are absorbing the live pattern. The benefit in human sacrifice could very well be in mythic threads, which is not to be underestimated as every difficulty reduction in an arete throw can be a significant boon. Also there is the notion that different kind of quintessence has different resonance. The essence gained from sacrificing humans would have entropic resonances, making them very usefull in destructive rituals, but less so in constructive ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well when I say evil I don't mean twirling your mustache evil, I mean someone whose behaviour could be called evil. Not the type of person who THINKS they're evil or revels in it; those are very rare.<br /> <br /> I suppose that you could use the sacrifice of the Borathean Princess in GoT as an example; her being burnt alive led to a huge thaw of the icy weather they were suffering from. This was a potent mythic thread, human sacrifice of a virgin, and a virgin with royal blood, and use of fire to destroy ice pushes this further. Burning a goat just wouldn't have cut it I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T05:19:59-07:00","id":1125855,"title":"","content":"You are right. Since all magic in Mage is <i>really</i> Chaos Magic deep inside, everyone who choses to use an evil paradigm is a tool. As is, admittedly, everyone who doesn't immediately believe in Chaos Magic.<br /> <br /> The two main categories of evil mages are nephandi and infernalists. Nephandi use evil paradigms because they are Always Chaotic Evil and evil is the whole point of being a Nephandi. They don't really need or have any reasons for using evil paradigms other than &quot;I'm a Nephandi&quot;. Infernalists don't really <i>need</i> to use evil paradigms, but they usually do because it pleases their patrons. And pleased demons may just give you a load of investments without taking a chunk of your soul, so it all works out.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hypernarrative&quot; mumbo jumbo is basically useless. It's a -1 modifier to your spellcasting, and the maximum possible modifier is -3. You know what also gives modifiers? Spending additional turns gives -1 per turn. Using personalized instrument gives -1. Being near a Node and/or doing research gives -1 to -3. Pretty much any time you might use a sacrifice to justify &quot;hypernarrative&quot; you might as well just spend another minute and get full -3 modifier with no sacrifices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12892,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","user":"Kammerer","date":". 08-07-2017, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T05:30:23-07:00","id":1125861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125827-what-s-the-point-of-being-bad?p=1125855#post1125855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Hypernarrative&quot; mumbo jumbo is basically useless. It's a -1 modifier to your spellcasting, and the maximum possible modifier is -3. You know what also gives modifiers? Spending additional turns gives -1 per turn. Using personalized instrument gives -1. Being near a Node and/or doing research gives -1 to -3. Pretty much any time you might use a sacrifice to justify &quot;hypernarrative&quot; you might as well just spend another minute and get full -3 modifier with no sacrifices.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've personally thought that this system needs tweaking. Difficulty breaks are just a bit too easy to come by when you have time to do things properly, and it's almost too easy to rack up 20 successes on something if you do all of the preparation you could ever need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T05:56:55-07:00","id":1125868,"title":"","content":"Perhaps to make a point. For example a Verbena might us a Progenitor or an Iterator as a source of quintessence as payback for that same progenitor using one of their own to power one of their horrible machines.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it's to kill without being wasteful. A dreamspeaker may consider their enemy to be perverting the power Mother Gaia has bestowed upon them, and seeks to redistribute this power by offering their enemy back into her embrace. Sacrifice her and allow the quintessence to be used for good, and thus their life would not have been wasted even if their living caused greater harm to Gaia.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the sacrifice is part of a way to save them. A Euthanatos might think a ritual is the proper way to provide one with the Good Death. Offering their soul to Kali to ensure it is properly reincarnated. The Quintessence left behind then is to be used by the Euthanatos mage in question. It is the last remnants of their being and thus must be used in order to allow the mage's avatar to properly reincarnate without ties to the previously doomed existence.<br /> <br /> There are loads of reasons a mage can incorporate ritual sacrifice into their crafts. You just need to think thematically rather than purely mechanically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T06:04:51-07:00","id":1125872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125827-what-s-the-point-of-being-bad?p=1125868#post1125868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are loads of reasons a mage can incorporate ritual sacrifice into their crafts. You just need to think thematically rather than purely mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like murdering someone's family in Skyrim, capturing their souls with the Black Star and Black Soul Gems, and crafting unique enchanted weapons named after them, and then killing them with the weapon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T06:29:38-07:00","id":1125878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125827-what-s-the-point-of-being-bad?p=1125872#post1125872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like murdering someone's family in Skyrim, capturing their souls with the Black Star and Black Soul Gems, and crafting unique enchanted weapons named after them, and then killing them with the weapon?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...Sorry, I'm not sure what point you're trying to make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T06:35:19-07:00","id":1125881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125827-what-s-the-point-of-being-bad?p=1125878#post1125878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Sorry, I'm not sure what point you're trying to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I mean doing it because you want to, for a thematic reason, rather than it being more powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T06:37:00-07:00","id":1125882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125827-what-s-the-point-of-being-bad#post1125827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or you could significantly reduce how much Quintessence you can get from animals, using a Vampire-type justification; yes an Elephant might be HUGE and it might seem logical that they'd contain a lot of Blood/Quintessence, but they are less energy-rich than a human; their soul is on a similar level to that of a dog or monkey, they just have a much much larger body to go with it. Simple, unintelligent animals would have a Quintessence of 1, smart animals (octopi, dogs, monkeys, elephants, dolphins) would have a Quintessence of 3 due to a slightly greater state of self-awareness. Now one human sacrifice is three times as potent as a dog sacrifice, which is a big enough gap that a sociopath might prefer a human...<br /> <br /> Have I missed some advantage to virgin sacrifice? Does it need a mechanical incentive?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd generally run Humans are pound for pound best for sacrifice unless something is hard and costly to aquire. Sacrifice is in value of what it costs to the sacrificer after all. So I'm probably giving guy who sacifices an elephant a shitload of quint because that's a whole story by itself, guy who takes over slaughterhouse who secretly adds in mystic trappings to make each death a kill well they may not get alot per cow but that's the value of industrialization!.<br /> <br /> As for why you'd pick virgins over other types, well first there's paradigm. Viriginity has all sorts of special symbolism in various paradigms and even your more scientific ones might want their sacrifices to lack external variables. Second if you are playing with Ressonence the quint would be marked by that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T06:41:15-07:00","id":1125884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125827-what-s-the-point-of-being-bad?p=1125882#post1125882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd generally run Humans are pound for pound best for sacrifice unless something is hard and costly to aquire. Sacrifice is in value of what it costs to the sacrificer after all. So I'm probably giving guy who sacifices an elephant a shitload of quint because that's a whole story by itself, guy who takes over slaughterhouse who secretly adds in mystic trappings to make each death a kill well they may not get alot per cow but that's the value of industrialization!.<br /> <br /> As for why you'd pick virgins over other types, well first there's paradigm. Viriginity has all sorts of special symbolism in various paradigms and even your more scientific ones might want their sacrifices to lack external variables. Second if you are playing with Ressonence the quint would be marked by that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't extracting Quintessence from each murdered cow mean some very hands-on processing? Plus, a dead cow is worth a decent amount of Quintessence, RAW, and moving that amount around on an industrial scale could mean movements of 10, 20, 50+ Quintessence... wouldn't that lead to crazy anomalies? I'm guessing that you could stop this with the right preparations of course. Also wouldn't it rob the cow's body of some of its vitality, make objectively worse meat?<br /> <br /> Oh I was being flippant when I referred to Virgin Sacrifice, it's just a common concept in magic that the sacrifice should be a virgin... but agreed, yes, lots of paradigms are looking for a pure maiden for resonance and symbolic power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T06:52:38-07:00","id":1125885,"title":"","content":"In some cases, a particular paradigm allows for more potent effects if sacrifice is involved. There's a Prime 3 effect in the Verbena tradbook that goes beyond the typical quintessence you'd get, and says that if you sacrifice a willing Awakened, you can raise a Node's rating. A bunch of fiction in the book describes a use of that rote, to empower a faltering Node on a Verbena farm. The Verbena paradigm is all about blood and sacrifice and it makes sense for them.<br /> <br /> From a mechanical perspective, you could easily argue this: &quot;Either Prime 3 allows you to sacrifice a willing Awakened to empower a Node or it doesn't. If it does, then you don't need to be Verbena to do it. If it doesn't, then the rote is broken and should include something else, like lots of Prime.&quot; That's all fair, but I would argue with both of those points.<br /> <br /> First, the Sphere system is a rough outline. Not everyone with Prime 3 can do everything listed under Prime 3, because they are limited by their paradigm - and no one has the paradigm of &quot;whatever it says in the Mage corebook&quot;. So it is in theory possible that Prime 3 does allow that effect and nobody but the Verbena - or another group whose paradigm is equally based around sacrifice - can actually cast it.<br /> <br /> Second, yes, you could imagine replicating this effect outside of that rote with Prime 5. But it seems odd that to do such an effect, you'd need the ability to enchant items - but by the Sphere system you would, because Prime 5 requires Prime 4. Think about it like Dark Ages: Mage with the Pillars system - where each group had their own path of powers. Hermetics threw fireballs by command of elemental forces via the Forma of Vires. Old Faith witches drew out the strength of Summer to do the same, and Valdaermen used the Hjaldar rune. So Hermetics who could throw fireballs could also refract light, but the witches and the Valdaermen couldn't - which makes sense based on their paradigms. So I don't mind bending the Sphere rules, as if a Verbena's Prime sphere is a little like a &quot;Verbena Prime&quot; Pillar with slight variance from what, say, a Progenitor might do.<br /> <br /> To bring it back to your original question: some paradigms would <i>require</i> sacrifice to produce typical effects, and sometimes effects beyond the common use of those Sphere levels. A Hermetic might call that Prime 3 rote &quot;evil&quot; but a Verbena certainly wouldn't. Power in Mage is based in beliefs and if you believe you need to sacrifice to get that power, that is actually true for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7356,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","user":"haldir2012","date":".  corrected from Life to Prime 08-07-2017, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T07:03:49-07:00","id":1125887,"title":"","content":"Some ancient gods that had...let's say, a different take on the value of human life...may prefer human sacrifice. Perhaps because they want those human souls to serve them in their realms (which does not necessarily equate to *hell*, it may actually be a relatively nice afterlife), or just because it demonstrates how much are your people willing to sacrifice. Of course, these two examples make more sense in the case of voluntary sacrifices, but, then, old civilizations often didn't care about free will or consent as much as us.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Plus, a dead cow is worth a decent amount of Quintessence, RAW, and moving that amount around on an industrial scale could mean movements of 10, 20, 50+ Quintessence... wouldn't that lead to crazy anomalies? I'm guessing that you could stop this with the right preparations of course. Also wouldn't it rob the cow's body of some of its vitality, make objectively worse meat?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you take it all, RAW, <i>the body of the cow would cease to exist </i>(and it's Vulgar, the Syndicate has better means to take advantage of industrialization). I think you may be confounding the Prime 3 rote that allows you to tape into the free quint that it's released after death with the &quot;higher levels&quot; that drain Quint that it's on the pattern. The lvl 3 can't absorb all that the body it's worth, it usually absorbs a variable quantity that it's related to the &quot;value&quot; of the act (or at least that's how things were in Revised), which means that a human would give more because we value human life more (yeah, it's a bit weird).<br /> <br /> But, yeah, I think the flesh left by the sacrifice should be worthless as food, albeit there's no rule about that (other that you can't create nourishing blood for a vampire without expending a lot of Quint, but that doesn't need to be related).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-07-2017, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T07:23:59-07:00","id":1125897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125827-what-s-the-point-of-being-bad?p=1125887#post1125887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some ancient gods that had...let's say, a different take on the value of human life...may prefer human sacrifice. Perhaps because they want those human souls to serve them in their realms (which does not necessarily equate to *hell*, it may actually be a relatively nice afterlife), or just because it demonstrates how much are your people willing to sacrifice. Of course, these two examples make more sense in the case of voluntary sacrifices, but, then, old civilizations often didn't care about free will or consent as much as us.<br /> <br /> If you take it all, RAW, <i>the body of the cow would cease to exist </i>(and it's Vulgar, the Syndicate has better means to take advantage of industrialization). I think you may be confounding the Prime 3 rote that allows you to tape into the free quint that it's released after death with the &quot;higher levels&quot; that drain Quint that it's on the pattern. The lvl 3 can't absorb all that the body it's worth, it usually absorbs a variable quantity that it's related to the &quot;value&quot; of the act (or at least that's how things were in Revised), which means that a human would give more because we value human life more (yeah, it's a bit weird).<br /> <br /> But, yeah, I think the flesh left by the sacrifice should be worthless as food, albeit there's no rule about that (other that you can't create nourishing blood for a vampire without expending a lot of Quint, but that doesn't need to be related).</div> </div> </div> </div>Noted, and I can see Mages using human sacrifice because they think it is better when in reality it isn't; everyone thinks their tool is the Bestest tool after all.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, the Syndicate can absorb Quintessence just through investing in a business after all (Primal Utility intensifies... can you imagine having the power to reshape the universe and using it to play around with cash you don't need?). I can't imagine anyone making a Quintessence Abattoir, except maybe on a rural farm where it could go unnoticed if you burn your dairy cows when they expire to release energy for the Mage who has made your farm their home.<br /> <br /> Agreed on nourishment; if you absorb all of the energy released when a cow dies, then you're not using that to feed people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T07:24:08-07:00","id":1125899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125827-what-s-the-point-of-being-bad?p=1125881#post1125881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh I mean doing it because you want to, for a thematic reason, rather than it being more powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages believe strongly in a specific paradigm (until they reach high Arete anyhow) and if your paradigms tells you human sacrifice is powerful then a) it will be powerful for you while other difficulty reductions may not be as potent (sucks to have this paradigm and b) you really think this is how it should work. I think Saikou gave some pretty good reasons why characters IC think a human sacrifice might be necessary or at least is an acceptable and sensible practice within their paradigm.<br /> <br /> People who rely on human sacrifice for power either have a paradigm that tells them this is how it is done (ancient aztec mages for example) or they are nephandi/infernalists who like to twirl their own mustache or that of their overlords. Sacrificing humans for quintessence is possible, but due to certain social factors (other mages being appaled and possibly hunting you down) just isn't worth pursuing even if you don't care for the moral implications yourself. Getting a goat is plain easier and has less risk of blowing up in your face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T08:53:19-07:00","id":1126319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125827-what-s-the-point-of-being-bad?p=1125899#post1125899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages believe strongly in a specific paradigm (until they reach high Arete anyhow) and if your paradigms tells you human sacrifice is powerful then a) it will be powerful for you while other difficulty reductions may not be as potent</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeaaaaaaaaaaah no. Paradigm does not override the mechanics. It may prevent you from doing something (like taking more time to do magic), but it can't make sacrifice better than it is for everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T09:05:42-07:00","id":1126324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125827-what-s-the-point-of-being-bad?p=1126319#post1126319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeaaaaaaaaaaah no. Paradigm does not override the mechanics. It may prevent you from doing something (like taking more time to do magic), but it can't make sacrifice better than it is for everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except where it suddenly can.<br /> <br /> Like the aformentioned more potent version of Heart's Blood in the Verbena Revised book. Or like the Void Engineers being able to drop the Gauntlet to Zero, with their Dimensional Science sphere. Which is nothing but paradigm. While the Mystic paradigm's can't, with Spirit. At least in M20.<br /> All the Technocracy-specific spheres simply boil down to their paradigms being different from the Mystic paradigms, and suddenly allowing for different mechanics, advantages and disadvantages, even down to how specific types of Wonders get created. Heck, it all started with the guidelines in the Revised mage Storyteller books on how to make new spheres based on Paradigm.. So...I guess that box of Pandora is opened. Now we just need to decide if it can move to a finer granularity than whole spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 08-08-2017, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T13:04:24-07:00","id":1126424,"title":"","content":"There was a rote in Dead Magic which required to rip the beating heart out of a human, and eat it in the name of Aztec Gods. It was *hard*, nasty, and very powerful going beyond normal rules...supposedly it involved actual intervention of the Aztecs gods, and could get specially nasty if you botched (beyond mere Paradox) because it would imply to suffer the anger of those gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T13:06:50-07:00","id":1126425,"title":"","content":"Theres also &quot;The Black Lotus&quot;, an Euthanatos Rote that involves self-sacrifice (you die). It may also be regarded as &quot;extra potent&quot;, beacuse it allowed to turn all your remaining Health and Quintessence in extra levels of Agg damage (on top of the normal damage rules).<br /> <br /> It's not like there isn't presedents for human sacrifice providing aditional power - just there are no rules about it, and we can't know for certain if this &quot;extra power&quot; comes from Paradigm, expectations, or whatever (but it does sound likely).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-08-2017, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T13:20:48-07:00","id":1126428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125827-what-s-the-point-of-being-bad?p=1126425#post1126425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theres also &quot;The Black Lotus&quot;, an Euthanatos Rote that involves self-sacrifice (you die). It may also be regarded as &quot;extra potent&quot;, beacuse it allowed to turn all your remaining Health and Quintessence in extra levels of Agg damage (on top of the normal damage rules).<br /> <br /> It's not like there isn't presedents for human sacrifice providing aditional power - just there are no rules about it, and we can't know for certain if this &quot;extra power&quot; comes from Paradigm, expectations, or whatever (but it does sound likely).</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 has mechanics for the Deathstrike; spells where you give up all of your remaining life-force to do something spectacular. You get a bunch of automatic successes and can use Sphere effects that go beyond your normal capabilities in some cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T13:39:09-07:00","id":1126436,"title":"","content":"I think your question is more, &quot;What's the point of human sacrifices versus any other foci?&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, the answer is, &quot;That is the way your magic works.&quot;<br /> <br /> Magic is kind of annoying in the fact you don't really get a choice how to do it. The Order of Hermes has people study decades with mathematics, textbooks, expensive laboratories, and so on to achieve the exact same results as the people who do it with a pocket calculator and crayons. However, that's pretty much how magic works as it is an intensely personal and religiously/philosophically based thing.<br /> <br /> The dude who believes his magic comes from Satan, even if he KNOWS it's all in his head, has to sacrifice people to do life magic because that's how it works. He can't just say, &quot;Well, why not have Life Magic work with some pills instead.&quot;<br /> <br /> Paradigm is a bitch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> 